{
  "run_id": "PMC12806431__problem_constrained__text_chunks__s2",
  "auditor": "trapi:gpt-5.6-sol_2026-07-09",
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Adding Cr to a high-entropy alloy can preserve toughness after thermal exposure and subsequent loading.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10759803::chunk::000::abstract::41e69f8748"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "The applicable initial material has a single-phase FCC or BCC solid-solution structure.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC6908586::chunk::000::abstract::78fa87d5e8",
        "PMC10759803::chunk::000::abstract::41e69f8748"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "The intervention is addition of Cr to the alloy.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed regime is thermal exposure at approximately 700 °C for approximately 1000 hours followed by mechanical loading.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC6908586::chunk::000::abstract::78fa87d5e8"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Cr can form a stable solid solution with the other alloying elements.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10759803::chunk::000::abstract::41e69f8748"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Cr addition can produce a secondary Laves phase in a BCC high-entropy alloy.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10759803::chunk::000::abstract::41e69f8748"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Exposure at 700 °C for 1000 hours can precipitate an additional BCC phase in an initially FCC Cr-Mn-Fe-Ni high-entropy alloy.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC6908586::chunk::000::abstract::78fa87d5e8"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Solid-solution hardening associated with Cr addition can increase strength.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10759803::chunk::000::abstract::41e69f8748"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "An intermetallic Laves phase can provide additional strengthening.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10759803::chunk::000::abstract::41e69f8748"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "A reticulated Laves-phase structure can improve ductility.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10759803::chunk::000::abstract::41e69f8748"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Cr addition can concurrently improve strength and ductility relative to a corresponding Cr-free alloy.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10759803::chunk::000::abstract::41e69f8748"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "After the stated thermal exposure and loading, the Cr-modified alloy will have greater toughness than the same alloy without Cr.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10759803::chunk::000::abstract::41e69f8748"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "After the stated thermal exposure and loading, the Cr-modified alloy will resist degradation better than the same alloy without Cr.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proper control is the same alloy without added Cr subjected to identical exposure and loading conditions.",
      "field": "baseline",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "There are exposure or loading limits beyond which the alloy will undergo significant degradation or failure.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "A controlled comparison of Cr-modified and Cr-free alloys under identical exposure and loading conditions can test the hypothesis.",
      "field": "falsification_experiment.design",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "TEM or SEM can assess the resulting microstructure, while tensile and hardness tests can assess mechanical properties.",
      "field": "falsification_experiment.measurements",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Failure of the Cr-modified alloy to improve toughness and degradation resistance over the Cr-free control would falsify the hypothesis.",
      "field": "falsification_experiment.falsification_rule",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
